cameronc@mindspring.com (Cam) wrote:

>Sometimes at work, after an extended period of non-use (vacation), a
>user's password mysteriously stops working.  I know we are using
>Digital's unix, but I have no idea what version.  No, I am not the
>admin, or an expert in unix, but I have heard that sometimes the
>passwd program will "expire" a passwrd after a certain length of time.
>Is there an option or setting somewhere to change the length of time?

Sounds like you are running C2 security on your system. This has
definable password lifetimes (often 3 months). Once it has expired,
the user may still change his password within another definable period
(often 1 month), before the account is locked.

You should go talk to your system administrator, but he/she sounds
like they are running quite normal security practices.

