> Hi
> 

...
> 
> Now we are still trying to tune the web cache, as the number of wired pages
> from vmstat is still high ( 25% ) of memory, and we never get it back when
> squid is killed. What is wired memory  and how can we see what processes are
> causing it to grow, so we can do something about them.
> 

With DU3.2C, there was a kernel memory problem related to NFS3 that
caused large quantities of CRED memory to be accumulated (look at
vmstat -M). There is a patch available. I've not noticed it with
any more recent versions of DU, however.

On a related matter, do you believe you have seen any unexplained
increase in virtual size of your applications? We have a large
application that gets larger but our efforts to locate a real leak
are in vain! I'm wondering about heap fragmentation... We see this
on DU 3.2C - haven't checked DU4 yet.

