On Thu, 30 Jan 1997, Amy Goodgame wrote:

> I have installed a Fast Etherworks pci 10/100 adapter in my
> alphaserver 2100 (running DU v4.0)  into the first pci expantion slot.
> In console mode when I do a show config everything looks fine the
> system knows its an ethernet port.  Hose 0, Bus 0 PCI in slot 6 module
> id is ewb0.0.0.6.0
> However, when I run netsetup, the network interfaces available for
> configuration are tu0 and sl0.  I already had tu0 configured before
> adding this new adapter.  I was expecting to see a tu1 interface.  Is
> there some setup utility that I need to run.   Thanks for any help.
> 
> Amy Goodgame
> <<goody@mindspring.com>>
 
Hi Amy,

You are probably need to modify system configuration file
in /usr/sys/conf.
I have the following there:

bus             pci0       at nexus?    
callout after_c "../bin/mkdata pci"
bus             psiop0     at pci0      slot  6 vector    psiopintr 
controller      scsi0      at psiop0    slot  0 
bus             isa0       at pci0      slot  7 
callout after_c "../bin/mkdata isa"
controller      gpc0       at isa0      slot  0 vector    gpcintr 
controller      ace0       at isa0      slot  2 vector    aceintr 
controller      ace1       at isa0      slot  3 vector    aceintr 
controller      lp0        at isa0      slot  4 vector    lpintr 
controller      fdi0       at isa0      slot  5 
device disk     fd0        at fdi0      drive     0 
controller      tu0        at pci0      slot  11 
controller      tga0       at pci0      slot  13 

Find out the slot number of new network card at pci bus
and add new line in config file,exmp:
controller	tu1	   at pci0	slot  14

Run doconfig -c <Name_of_the_config_file>.

If You dont know the slot number try the following procedure:
mv /vmunix /vmunix.sav
cp /genvmunix /vmunix
doconfig
mv /usr/sys/<SYSTEM_NAME>/vmunix /
shutdown -r now

The first method I used to install a Turbochannel network card.

Reply on any questions.

Regards,
Sergey





