> Vivek Baveja wrote:
> > 
> > Can any one tell me how bad could .forward and .rhosts file could be for
> > making system safe from hackers
> 
> .rhosts should also be safe - it's best kept with 0600 permissions
> (-rw------), and you should be careful which hosts you trust - specify
> hosts explicitly and don't use wildcards if possible.

I wouldn't use .rhosts at all if you can help it.  The authentication
protocol used is extremely weak.  A remote system can pass itself off as
one of the trusted systems in your .rhosts and forge your login name to
get in.  Another common trick is to place a permissive .rhosts in a
world- or group-writable home directory to gain entry to an account.

