>If we do a "sh dev" at the boot prompt, it is recognized as MKA300 with
>the correct ID string.
>But if we boot the machine, it is not known anymore. uerf only shows
>the EXB8505, not the second one, as shown in the appending error log.
>What might be the reason? Is the EXB8500 not supported anymore?

If you had this effect with DUNIX 3.2, I would answer, that the
Exabyte is recognized by the system, but not compiled into the
kernel (-> booting with /genvmunix, doconfig, copy the new kernel
to /vmunix and voila). Nevertheless the tapedrive should work
even without doing this.

But to my knowledge this has been changed in version 4.0 (I have
no experience with it, I only heart about). The kernel should
recognize all the disks and tapedrives and load the modules.

You have already tried to do a 'MAKEDEV tz3' to build the special
files for the tape and to access the tape? This should be
possible even the kernel does not list this tapedrive at
startup. (At least this is the case in 3.2)

