Frank Jendraszak (fjj@sashimi.wwa.com) wrote:
: How or where do I add a line to start up a process at boot time?
:
: i.e., I'd like to start my own daemon at boot time.
:
: Do I put it into rc.config, rc.config.site? What is the syntax?

You have two choices: write a script like you find in /sbin/init.d/ to
start/stop your daemon anmd symlink it to the directory for the run
level that you want, or put a line in /etc/inittab. "man rc3" will
tell you about the first option, "man inittab" about the second.

rc.config and rc.config.site are where environment variables used by
the scripts in /sbin/init.d are defined. "man rcmgr" for details.

Stephen
