Jean,

Evaluate your backup products based on the features and benefits each 
provides.  Every software product has a certain number of problems, and
NetWorker is no exception.  NetWorker's bug count is comparable to
other products of similar complexity.  We strive for high quality in
our products, and to fix problems quickly when they arise.

Granted, I am biased in that I work for Digital in it's NetWorker 
engineering group.  But to eliminate a product from consideration
because of an offhand comment that it is "riddled with bugs" is not
in your own best interest.

In making your decision, you may be interested in a recent Legato
press release about the performance of an upcoming future release of 
NetWorker on Digital UNIX.  The full press release can be found at 
http://www.legato.com/press/digora_pr.html.  The second paragraph of
the release reads:

 "Working together, Legato and DIGITAL have demonstrated a "hot" Oracle
 backup of 420 gigabytes per hour while attaining a restore rate of 136
 gigabytes per hour. Conducted jointly by Legato and Digital Equipment
 Corporation at DIGITAL's Palo Alto facility, the tests measured the
 maximum transfer rate achieved in backing up and restoring an Oracle
 database using Oracle's EBU (Enterprise Backup Utility) and DIGITAL's
 NetWorker (jointly developed by Legato and DIGITAL) running on a
 DIGITAL AlphaServer 8400 with eight 300 MHz Alpha CPUs, 8gb of memory,
 440GB StorageWorks' Disk Subsystem, and 15 StorageTek Redwood tape
 subsystems."

Good luck in finding the best solution for your needs.

Regards,

Wes



