>from "sizer -wk" that the keyboard type is being determined properly but for 
>some reason the "console language variable" seems to be US (36) on most of our 
>machines rather than UK (38).  Can anybody tell me how I go about setting this 
>variable?

Sure, it depends on the hardware platform, so you'll want to find the
hardware manual, and look up language settings. For example on my
AS200 4/233 you go to console mode:

>>> set language

This clears the language environment variable.

>>> init

With the language environment variable cleared, when you do the init
it brings up the language selection menu, and you can choose UK
or whatever you like. On the sandpipers I think the manual lists the
values of the language variable, and you just set them. Anyway you
get the idea.

