Brian Bouchard wrote:
> I have a Dec3000 M800 Alpha system, running OSF/1 V2.0 (Rel. 240).  After a
> period of time the system will not allow any further connections (telnet,
> ftp, etc...).  But if you have a connection already open before the lock
> out you can work as normal.  Anybody have any ideas as to why we keep
> getting locked out???  We can't seem to find anything out of  the ordinary,
> we have to reboot each time it happens.

First see if inetd is running.  If not, the problem is that inetd
exited.
If it's running, you might want to check in various logs to see if it is
complaining about anything.  Are you running a web server on the box, by
any chance?  The reason I ask is that we had similar problems that we
finally
tracked down to an interesting behavior of inetd on DU:  it has a
built-in
sanity timer and will cop an insanity plea if it receives more than 
X connections per minute (default X=500 on 3.2G).

Cheers,
Todd



