Craig Paul wrote:
> 
> How does one configure sendmail to deliver a user's e-mail to their
> home directory (rather than /var/spool/mail/<username>)?
> 
> Thank you!


1.Create a .forward file that contains "| /usr/lib/mh/slocal -user XXX"

2. Create a directory with the various inboxes.

3. Create a .decxmailcheck file that contains the following pattern:

inbox $HOME/mailbox_dir/inbox
folder-name1 $HOME/mailbox_dir/folder-name1
folder-name2 $HOME/mailbox_dir/folder-name2
folder-name3 $HOME/mailbox_dir/folder-name3

4. Create a .maildelivery file with the following pattern:
from    PATTERN    >       ?       $HOME/mailbox_dir/folder
from    PATTERN    ^       ?       "/usr/lib/mh/rcvstore +folder"
*       -         >        ?       $HOME/mailbox_dir/inbox
default -       >       ?         /usr/spool/mail/XXX

The first line will put an incoming email in one of your inboxes
and if you have a corresponding line in your .decxmailcheck file
then that folder will be highlighted in dxmail to show new mail.

The second will put an incoming email directly into the mail
folder but won't notify you.

The third line will put all unmatched patterns into your new 
inbox and the 4th line is a safety line in case your $home/maildir
gets trashed.

I really recomend the the MH & XMH book from O'Reilly.

Charlie


PS I hope that this helps. Honestly, I did not really have the time to
write it!!!!
