Mike Plante wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> Anyone out there having trouble with zombie processes created when LAT
> is used for logins via terminals? We're running DU 4.0A and are seeing
> an inordinate number of zombie processes appear when users are prematurely
> disconnected from their LAT ports for one reason or another (nothing specific).
> 
> They cannot be killed either. Rebooting's about it as far as clearing them.
> I suppose they're waiting for I/O but something locked up on these ports
> and I can't figure it. pty's are fine though - just LAT.

Yup. I had it under 3.2C. It was caused by some old DECserver 100s that
didn't have hardware flow control lines, so the terminal server couldn't
detect when a terminal was shut off, and wouldn't allow DU to release
the connection. You can free the LAT line by resuming the session on the
terminal. Around here it is usually because a student hit ^S
accidentally and then freaked out.

Thankfully I just convinced them to throw the DECserver 100s out.

