organization: University of California, Berkeley
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


A while back I wrote a document about how to create a dataless
environment on DEC Unix (V2.x and V3.x) and I posted the document
here. Based on the comments I received, many people followed this
approach with great success. Now people are asking me whether this
approach still works on DEC Unix 4.x. My problem is that I no longer
have anything to do with managing a DEC Unix environment so I frankly
have no idea whether it works or not.

So, I'm asking for someone to come forward to volunteer to try my
approach and to take over support for the document. Supporting
the document means both making sure it's right and putting it
somewhere easily accessible on the Internet. If you want to do this
then you can also take all future credit for the approach and do
whatever you want with the document. I have no interest in this
anymore.

Note that DEC started supporting a dataless environment in DEC Unix
V4.x but, unless I'm mistaken, my approach is much more general
and much simplier.

The document currently lives in

	ftp://s2k-ftp.cs.berkeley.edu//pub/personal/forrest/remote.mounting

Please contact me via-email (forrest@cs.berkeley.edu) if you're
interested.

