In article <t0enfwe3iw.fsf@purcell.ikp.liu.se>, Erik Persson <erik@ikp.liu.se> writes:
:1. Can the AS4000 use a serial console?

  Yes.  (This should be covered in the owner's guide.)

:2. All the Suns that I administer responds to some kind of break
:   sequence (break on a serial terminal and Stop-A on the regular
:   keyboard) upon the execution of the operating system will be
:   suspended and the boot monitor is entered....  This feature is
:   very useful if you have remote access to the serial port and
:   the system for some reason cannot be halted. The question is
:   now if the DEC3000 and/or 4000 has this kind of feature and
:   if this is the case - how can I enable it. 

   Various Sun systems seem to use the keyboard connection as a
   halt signal.

   Most recent Digital VAX and Alpha systems use the <BREAK> key
   (via the console serial line) to halt the system -- a <BREAK>
   is a deliberately induced framing error.  Relatively few of
   the newer systems support the <CTRL/P> halt sequence (this is
   more commonly used on older VAX systems), but if memory serves,
   the AlphaServer 4x00 SRM console does support <CTRL/P>.

   Check the owner's guide and the SRM (console) documentation
   for configuration information.  As part of this, you need to
   switch the CONSOLE from GRAPHICS to SERIAL.

