Lukas Rosenthaler (rosenth@foto.chemie.unibas.ch) wrote:
> Hi,
>
> a simple question:
>
> 1) Is is possible to use 2 different TCP/IP adresses on one ethernet
>    interface under DUNIX 4.0 ?
>
> if 1) == yes : Who has the setup of the 2 adresses to be done? Is there
>                somewhere a simple description?

It is possible. Read the man page of ifconfig carefully. To enable this
feature after bootup, you should enter an entry in /etc/rc.config which
looks like this:

IFCONFIG_0="1.1.1.1 netmask 255.0.0.0"
IFCONFIG_1="alias 2.2.2.2 netmask 255.0.0.0"

Hope this helps

  Gregor

