Jeff Shervey wrote:
> With DEC UNIX 3.2 how can I search a bunch of subdirectories for a
> certain file that contains certain text.
> I'm trying this command with no luck:
> 
> find . -name *.sql -print | grep -i "duplicate" *.pls

Close.  Try:
	find . -name \*.sql -print | xargs grep -i duplicate /dev/null

The /dev/null is to ensure that grep will tell you the filename.
Without it, if the last call to grep has only one file, you won't
know the filename.
